# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefix-tiers development window (the preconverted GDN checkpoints and the host KV tier; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are
# resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head (sed -i 's/tp4-prefix-tiers-1/<tag>/' *.env); every later job serves that one
# image. A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# A1 (STOP): the AUDITED ATTACH of the tier profile (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tier-audit), the production stack (Lever N + prefix reuse + W2 + engine reuse) plus exactly the host tier and the preconverted checkpoints with every instrument on
# (scripts/ci/make_prefix_tier_profiles.py: QWEN_PREFIX_HOST_TIER_GIB=32 beside the 8 GiB checkpoint store, HOST_TIER_AUDIT, HOST_TIER_VERIFY=all, CKPT_PRECONVERTED, CKPT_PRECONVERTED_AUDIT). The smoke is production's own
# tests (warmup, one coding answer, eight 4k-token code users, eight 3.5k-token steady users), unsalted, so no tier traffic: this job proves the ENGINE ATTACHES with the tier's device IO and serves as it did. READ in this order and stop at the first
# failure: (1) the launched argv and the profile's env (the tier names above, no waiver, gate only); (2) ENGAGED: '[PINDIAG] prefix: install' with sticky=1, the model graft's '[PINDIAG] prefix: model warm' with a restore path of h2d
# (the preconverted checkpoints need it; the model refuses to start otherwise), '[PINDIAG] prefix: host tier IO attached block_bytes=<n> tensors=<n> chips=4' and '[PINDIAG] prefix: host tier on gib=32.00 kv_gib=24.00 ... verify=all audit=1';
# (3) the smoke clean (c2_smoke_check), every answer complete, no AssertionError/Traceback, no stall; (4) the ledger's free DRAM per chip after the attach, against the production profile's (the tier is host RAM: no device allocation, the raw ops run no
# program); (5) the 'tier rss=' log line's host RSS and available memory, recorded (the slab grows with use, nothing is reserved up front). Unqualified: a measurement, never evidence. Duration (estimate): 120 minutes. Stop rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tier-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_equal,coding
C2_BOX_MINUTES=120
